BT /F1 11 Tf 40 750 Td 14 TL
(St Xavier Institute of Medical Laboratory Technology) Tj T*
(Affiliated to the State University of Health Sciences) Tj T*
(Accredited by NAAC with grade A and recognised by the UGC) Tj T*
(Annual Report and Self Study Report) Tj T*
(IQAC feedback and criteria documents are enclosed) Tj T*
(Placement cell report, prospectus and certificate annexures) Tj T*
(All rights reserved. Published for public information.) Tj T*
(Placement and Internship Policy 2023-24) Tj T*
(Short Title and Commencement) Tj T*
(These rules shall be called the Placement and Internship Policy of the University.) Tj T*
(They apply to every student admitted to a bachelor programme in the faculty of allied health sciences, including the Medical Laboratory Technology programme.) Tj T*
(Definitions) Tj T*
(Placement cell means the university office responsible for coordinating internships, employer relations, and student placement records.) Tj T*
(Eligible student means a student who has completed the prescribed coursework, has no pending disciplinary action, and has registered with the placement cell.) Tj T*
(Internship means supervised practical training in a hospital laboratory or an approved diagnostics facility for the duration prescribed by the curriculum.) Tj T*
(Registration) Tj T*
(Every eligible student shall register with the placement cell before the published deadline, submit an updated curriculum vitae, and attend the pre-placement orientation conducted by the cell.) Tj T*
(A student who does not register by the deadline may participate only if the cell certifies that seats remain available with a participating employer.) Tj T*
(Obligations of the student) Tj T*
(The student shall attend every interview for which the cell nominates the student, maintain the confidentiality of employer information, and accept the offer made through the cell in good faith.) Tj T*
(The student shall not approach an employer directly for a role that the cell has announced, and shall report every offer received to the cell within three working days.) Tj T*
(Obligations of the employer) Tj T*
(The employer shall share an accurate job description, the location of the posting, the compensation offered, and the expected date of joining.) Tj T*
(The employer shall not withdraw an offer after acceptance except for a documented reason communicated in writing to the cell and the student.) Tj T*
(Attendance and leave) Tj T*
(During the internship the student shall maintain the attendance required by the host laboratory and shall apply for leave through both the host supervisor and the faculty coordinator.) Tj T*
(Absence without sanctioned leave may result in the internship being treated as incomplete and may require the student to repeat the affected rotation.) Tj T*
(Assessment) Tj T*
(The host supervisor shall submit a structured assessment covering laboratory safety, technical competence, record keeping, and professional conduct.) Tj T*
(The faculty coordinator shall combine that assessment with the student's logbook and viva voce performance to determine the final grade.) Tj T*
(Grievances) Tj T*
(A student who believes that a placement decision was arbitrary may submit a written representation to the placement cell within seven working days.) Tj T*
(The cell shall consider the representation, record its reasons, and communicate the decision to the student within fourteen working days.) Tj T*
(Review) Tj T*
(The academic council shall review this policy at least once every three years and may amend it after consulting the placement cell and the faculties.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
